  "pr": {
    "title": "test(adhd): enforce activity payload privacy",
    "body": "## Problem\\nActivity Capture accepts events that may include filenames, prompt text, code snippets, or other content-bearing fields. ADHD Engine activity payloads must remain content-free and aggregate-only.\\n\\n## Fix\\n- Strip content-bearing file/prompt/code fields from normalized workspace activity.\\n- Ensure pending tracker activity stores only aggregate-safe file activity fields.\\n- Keep ADHD Engine activity client payload construction allowlisted.\\n- Add focused tests proving forbidden fields are not forwarded or stored.\\n\\n## Test Plan\\n- Validate Task Packet JSON and schema.\\n- Run focused Activity Capture tests.\\n- Run compileall, git diff --check, and pre-commit on changed files.",
    "base": "main"
  },
